{#
  « Aucune tâche planifiée réelle n'a été détectée » — the warning a
  configuration screen owes its administrator when the feature it
  configures depends on an INSTANT.

  A real crontab is a REQUIREMENT (ARCHITECTURE.md §8.5): the in-request
  fallback that used to run one scheduler slice on the back of a visitor's
  page load is gone, deliberately, because a safety net that hides the
  failure it catches is why one production installation ran for days on a
  crontab entry that executed nothing. So without it the timed function
  does not run late — it does not run at all, and that is what this says.

  Three screens warned; five that needed it did not, the emergency-duty
  redirection among them (issue #248). Two of the three also still
  described the old visit-driven fallback as though it were there. One
  partial rather than eight copies, so the next screen that gains a timed
  feature has one line to write and cannot word the warning differently —
  nor keep an old one true-sounding after the mechanism behind it went.

  Parameters
  ----------
  cron_detected : bool     the verdict, from Core\Scheduler\CronHealth
                           ::detectedForConfigScreen()
  feature       : string   what does not run, as a French noun phrase
                           subject of « … ne fonctionnent pas » below —
                           e.g. « Les rappels d'évènement ». Kept per
                           screen because a generic « les tâches
                           planifiées » says nothing to the person reading
                           THIS page.
  consequence   : string   what that costs here, one sentence. Optional.
#}
{% if not cron_detected %}
    <output class="alert alert-warning d-block">
        <strong>Aucune tâche planifiée réelle n'a été détectée.</strong>
        {{ feature }} ne fonctionnent alors pas du tout : le crontab du
        serveur est le seul mécanisme qui les déclenche, et il n'existe
        plus de rattrapage à l'occasion d'une visite du site.
        {% if consequence is defined and consequence %}{{ consequence }}{% endif %}
        Faites appeler <code>public/cron.php</code> toutes les minutes
        (<code>* * * * * php /chemin/vers/le/site/public/cron.php</code>).
    </output>
{% endif %}
